Q6. SQL Queries and OLAP

Code

  CREATE DATABASE IF NOT EXISTS prac;
  USE prac;

  CREATE TABLE sales (
     sale_id      INT,
     product_name VARCHAR(30),
     quantity     INT,
     amount       INT
  );

  INSERT INTO sales VALUES
  (1,'Pen',10,100),
  (2,'Book',5,250),
  (3,'Pen',20,200);

  SELECT * FROM sales;

  SELECT SUM(amount) AS total_sales FROM sales;

  SELECT product_name, SUM(amount) AS total_amount
  FROM sales
  GROUP BY product_name;

Role of OLAP in analysing sales data
OLAP (Online Analytical Processing) is used to analyse large amounts of data from different
points of view.

 • Multidimensional analysis. Sales can be viewed by dimensions such as product, time
   period and region.
 • Roll-up and drill-down. Roll-up shows yearly sales from monthly sales. Drill-down gives
   the reverse. Slice and dice show the sales of one product or one city, and pivot rotates the
   view.
 • Fast summaries. Totals and averages are returned quickly from a data warehouse that
   stores historical data.
 • Trend analysis. Past sales can be compared across months and years to find patterns and
   forecast demand.
 • Decision making. Management can find best-selling products, weak months and trends,
   and plan stock and offers.

